# Food & Drink Editorial Rules

The homepage and the Food & Drink guide serve **different purposes**.

## Homepage — today's front page

Show **exactly 8 featured** restaurants. Inspire discovery in under 10 seconds — not a directory.

**Hard rules:**
- Never repeat a cuisine or category in the featured 8
- Never show two coffee shops, two pizza places, or two bakeries
- Never repeat the same restaurant anywhere else on the homepage (cross-section dedupe)
- Every pick should offer a **different dining experience**
- Chains rank below outstanding local restaurants unless truly exceptional or locally iconic

**Typical spread:** coffee · bakery · burgers · Mexican · sushi · pizza · steakhouse · dessert

Implementation: `selectHomepageRecommendationCards()` with `depth: 8`, `maxPerFingerprint: 1`.

## Food & Drink guide — complete dining guide

Kindred's **definitive local dining guide** for every city served.

**Do NOT** impose artificial limits (50, 100, 250). Include every restaurant within **~25 miles** that meets editorial standards. If 163 qualify, show 163.

**Organize** into editorial category sections (see `FOOD_DRINK_GUIDE_SECTIONS` in `foodDrinkGuide.ts`).

**Every listing includes:** editorial summary, full article, atmosphere, signature dishes, what locals order, best time to visit, nearby suggestions, Open in Maps, official website, editorial closing note.

Implementation: `organizeFoodDrinkGuide()` — full qualifying pool, grouped by section, no publication cap.

## Shared catalog sync (server-side only)

Food & Drink venues live in the **Kindred Editorial Database** (`food_drink_catalog`).
See `kindred-editorial-database.mdc` for Source Manager, lifecycle, and provenance rules.

Foursquare is **never** queried per user, per session, or during edition build.

| Schedule | Mode | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| First cron for a metro | `full` | Initial metro-area import |
| Daily ~3:15 UTC | `incremental` | New/changed restaurants (~24h discovery) |
| Weekly Sunday ~4:30 UTC | `full` | Reconciliation, closures, duplicates, missed venues |

**Edition reads:** `getLocalPlaces()` → `loadFoodDrinkCatalogPlaces()` (DB only).
**Metro enrollment:** `registerFoodDrinkMetro()` on edition build — no provider calls.
**Scheduled sync:** `sync-food-drink-catalog` edge function (CRON_SECRET).

New restaurants pass verification before publication. Homepage still shows **exactly 8**
diverse featured picks — never auto-promote a venue because it is new.

## Engineering pointers

| Concern | Module |
| --- | --- |
| Homepage featured 8 | `recommendations.ts` → `selectHomepageRecommendationCards` |
| Guide sections | `foodDrinkGuide.ts` → `organizeFoodDrinkGuide` |
| Fingerprint variety | `foodDrinkCuration.ts` → `curateFoodDrinkEdition` |
| 25-mile radius | `localDiscoveryScope.ts` |
| Catalog sync | `places/foodDrinkCatalogSync.ts` + `sync-food-drink-catalog` |
| Provider retrieval | Scheduled sync only — `foursquareProvider.ts` (`full` / `incremental`) |
| Edition read path | `places/index.ts` → `loadFoodDrinkCatalogPlaces` |
| Article fields | `discoveryArticles.ts` → `composePlaceDiscoveryArticle` |
| Cross-section dedupe | `sectionAllocator.ts` |

**The Kindred test:** Would an experienced food editor put this on tomorrow's front page (homepage) or in the city dining guide (See All)?
